WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
A letter appears in a fast stream. You spot it.
The next task should be easy.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
But another target, arriving a fraction of a second later,
can be oddly difficult to report.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
In 1992, researchers documented this brief
attentional blink in a controlled visual task.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Later studies found that changing attention—
even adding task-irrelevant mental activity—could alter the effect.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Intensive meditation research also measured changes.
It did not test a twelve-minute branded audio program.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Explore the source, try a free reflection,
and judge tools by what evidence actually supports.
